Z||000000||mshill||03-14-2000||03:28 PM||||In the auto parts store this morning.  While looking for the water pump outlet hose (BTW I will have to go to the dealer for it) some bubba (yes, we have some in California) pipes up...<P>"So there's still some of those around, huh?"<P>(me) "Yes, quite a few, I have two of them."<P>"My brother bought one of those for his daughter when they first came out in, uh, '82."<P>(me) "You mean '84 right.  That was the first year they were produced."<P>"Yea, whatever.  They ended up taking sending it back because of the 'Lemon Law'.  The brakes went bad, the clutch was bad, and the engine ended up having a cracked block."<P>(me) "Oh, was it a 4 cylinder?"<P>"No, I am pretty sure it was a V8."<P>(me) "Ok. So what's that can you got there?"<P>"Just a little Bondo for my truck." (As he <BR>points to what looks like about a 100 year old Ford truck, whose primary color is <BR>primer gray, and trimmed out nicely in red crumbling rust.)<BR>||||reg||10
